cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MIDAS in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MIDAS: Mineral Interface Dynamics and apparent-Age Simulation"
authors:
  - family-names: Stroh
    given-names: Annalena
    affiliation: "Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz (JGU)"
  - family-names: Moulas
    given-names: Evangelos
    affiliation: "Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz (JGU)"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-28
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/AnStroh/MIDAS"
abstract: >
  MIDAS (Mineral Interface Dynamics and apparent-Age Simulation) is an
  interface-limited crystal-growth model (a moving-boundary problem) for a
  mineral growing/resorbing in a surrounding matrix phase, coupled to
  major- and trace-element diffusion and partitioning between the two. The
  example provided is a garnet-biotite pair (major elements Mg-Fe; trace
  elements Lu, Hf, Mn), built for modeling Lu-Hf garnet geochronology,
  apparent ages and interface (growth/resorption) velocities over a
  metamorphic P-T-t path. Provided as MATLAB, GNU Octave, and interactive
  GUI (MATLAB App Designer) versions.
keywords:
  - geochronology
  - Lu-Hf
  - apparent ages
  - garnet
  - crystal growth
  - Stefan problem
  - moving boundary
  - diffusion
  - petrology